---
// src/pages/bucknell/anop-400.astro  →  arizvi.com/bucknell/anop-400
// ANOP 400: how the term runs, where the clients come from, how it's graded, and what happens when it goes wrong. Not linked from the nav; sends noindex.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Section from '../../components/Section.astro';
import CourseHeader from '../../components/CourseHeader.astro';
import FourSteps from '../../components/FourSteps.astro';
import CourseNav from '../../components/CourseNav.astro';
import Gantt from '../../components/Gantt.astro';
import HandedIn from '../../components/HandedIn.astro';
import { pack } from '../../data/packs/anop-400';
import { course, bucknellColours } from '../../data/bucknell';

const c = course('anop-400');

// The ANOP 400 term, week by week.
const term = [
  { label: 'Scope', bars: [[1, 3]] as [number, number][] },
  { label: 'Data and discovery', bars: [[4, 6]] as [number, number][] },
  { label: 'Modeling', bars: [[7, 10]] as [number, number][] },
  { label: 'Recommendation', bars: [[11, 13]] as [number, number][] },
  { label: 'Delivery', bars: [[14, 14]] as [number, number][] },
  { label: 'With the client', marks: [{ w: 1 }, { w: 3 }, { w: 8 }, { w: 11 }, { w: 14 }] },
  { label: 'Team stand-ups', ticks: Array.from({ length: 13 }, (_, i) => i + 1) },
];

const brief = [
  ['The client', 'A regional credit union with 9 branches. Contact: the head of lending.'],
  ['The decision', 'Which members to call in the month before their car loan ends, so they refinance here.'],
  ['The data', '3 years of auto loans, about 40,000 rows. Member IDs replaced before the file reaches the team.'],
  ['The deliverable', 'A ranked call list for 1 month, and a 2-page memo on what a call is worth and where the cutoff sits.'],
  ['Success', 'A backtest on the last 6 months: how many of the members who refinanced elsewhere the list would have flagged in time.'],
  ['The client gives', '5 meetings (weeks 1, 3, 8, 11 and 14), 2 staff interviews in week 5, a 30-minute handover, a named contact, and the data by week 4.'],
];

---
<Base title="ANOP 400" description="ANOP 400, the Business Analytics Practicum, as Ali Rizvi would run it at Bucknell: the term, the clients, the grading, and what happens when a project goes wrong." noindex accent={bucknellColours} up={['/bucknell/', 'All courses']}>
  <CourseHeader course={c} facts={[
    ['Format', '14 weeks, teams of 4 or 5 with a client each'],
  ]}>
    <p class="practice"><span class="label">A sample</span>ANOP 400 already has an instructor and a client pipeline, and I would work with both. I would run a section the way I ran Waterloo's capstone seminar.</p>
  </CourseHeader>

  <FourSteps steps={[
    'Each team delivers a model and a recommendation, presented to the client in week 14. The charter signed in week 3 says what that will be.',
    'Every team follows the same term on its own client\'s problem, with a 15-minute stand-up each week.',
    'I ran 3 sections of Waterloo\'s capstone seminar on live client projects. The charter comes from my A/B testing work: agree on the metric and the stopping rule before you start.',
    'Each term I would sit down with the course\'s instructor, go through the peer evaluations, stand-up notes and client feedback, and see what worked and what did not.',
  ]} />

  <Section title="Week by week" id="term">
    <Gantt title="The ANOP 400 term, week by week" weeks={14} rows={term}
      caption="Client meetings in weeks 1, 3, 8, 11 and 14, and a weekly stand-up with me." />
  </Section>

  <Section title="Where the projects come from" id="clients">
    <div class="grid"><div class="span-8">
      <p>The course already has a client pipeline, and I would work within it. If more clients are needed, I would look to local businesses, Bucknell's Small Business Development Center, alumni companies and regional nonprofits, starting the term before.</p>
      <p>Each client signs the charter and a data agreement, once the university has cleared the template. Customer IDs are removed before files reach students, and students sign an NDA where asked.</p>
    </div></div>
    <div class="grid" style="margin-top: 2rem;"><div class="span-8">
      <p class="label">A sample brief · fictional</p>
      <div class="kv brief">
        {brief.map(([k, v]) => (<><p class="label">{k}</p><p>{v}</p></>))}
      </div>
    </div></div>
  </Section>

  
  
  <HandedIn pack={pack} />

  <Section title="The playbook" id="playbook">
    <div class="grid"><div class="span-8">
      <ol>
        <li><strong>The client has not signed by week 3.</strong> The charter is graded on the team's draft, and the team starts on the plan B dataset while I chase the signature.</li>
        <li><strong>The client goes quiet.</strong> It happens, and usually around week 9. The charter names a plan B dataset in the same domain, and the team switches at that week's stand-up without losing the week.</li>
        <li><strong>The data is late.</strong> The week 4 deadline is in the charter. The team starts on a public stand-in the same day, and the client's file replaces it when it lands.</li>
        <li><strong>A teammate disappears.</strong> Stand-up records and the week 7 peer evaluation make it visible early. I have the conversation in week 7, and the grade follows the record.</li>
        <li><strong>The client changes the question.</strong> The charter is re-signed, and the report keeps the week 3 version as what changed and why.</li>
        <li><strong>The model says nothing useful.</strong> That is a finding. The memo says what the data can and cannot support, and what to collect next year.</li>
        <li><strong>The client cannot make week 14.</strong> The presentation goes ahead with me in the client's chair, the client gets the recording and the report, and the 45% is unchanged.</li>
      </ol>
    </div></div>
  </Section>

  <CourseNav current={c.slug} />
</Base>
